{
  "version": 8,
  "name": "WhereWild Standard OpenFreeMap (Dark)",
  "metadata": {
    "ww:note": "Recolor of WhereWild's own OpenMapTiles-schema standard-light.json layer structure using real values from OpenFreeMap's 'bright' (light) and 'dark' style JSON (github.com/hyperknot/openfreemap-styles, MIT repo license; individual styles' own LICENSE.md: 'bright' is a fork of openmaptiles/osm-bright-gl-style, BSD-3-Clause code / CC-BY 4.0 design; 'dark' is (c) MapTiler.com & OpenMapTiles contributors / CartoDB Inc., BSD-3-Clause, derived from the same CartoDB Basemaps lineage as our standard-light.json). Both source style JSONs target genuine unmodified OpenMapTiles schema (confirmed via their actual source-layer names matching ours exactly), so unlike variable-light/ standard-versatiles-*, this needed no schema porting \u2014 values are ported onto our own smaller layer set (32 layers vs. their 47-119) rather than importing their full layer stack, and a handful of our own layers with no direct source equivalent (scrub/wetland/rock/ferry/rail-dashline/road-path) use WhereWild's own values in the same tint idiom as standard-light.json, same as that file's own extras."
  },
  "glyphs": "{fontstack}/{range}.pbf",
